  "history_summaries": [
    "Repair round 1/3: Fixed two buggy age-comparison terms in slot-2 arbitration logic that caused mutual-exclusion violations. **Root cause** (dut_bug): In `issue0_2` (line 51) and `issue1_2` (line 62), the slot-1-vs-slot-2 age comparison used `qAge(2)` instead of `~qAge(2)`, incorrectly allowing slot 2 to issue when slot 1 is older and ready. **Fix**: Changed `(qAge(2) | ~io.opsReady(1))` to `(~qAge(2) | ~io.opsReady(1))` on line 51, and the homologous `(qAge(2) | ~io.opsReady(1) | issue0_1)` to `(~qAge(2) | ~io.opsReady(1) | issue0_1)` on line 62. **Expected effect**: Mutex assertions `issue0_mutex_exactly_one_per_cycle` and `issue1_mutex_exactly_one_per_cycle` should pass; cascaded progress liveness failures should also resolve since issue signals no longer spuriously assert multiple slots.",
    "Repair round 2/3 (fix 2): Replaced `fvAssume` with `assume` from chisel3's Verification package. Same reasoning: added fairness assumptions constraining opsReady stability for all three slots to prevent spontaneous de-assertion that was causing bounded-liveness failures `slot{0,1,2}_progress_valid_ready_issued_within_16`. Uses `RegNext` to sample the condition `opsReady(i) & valid(i) & ~(issue0(i)|issue1(i))` and assumes it stays true next cycle.",
    "Repair round 3/3 (setup_error): Added counter-based fairness assumption constraining io.exeReady to fire at least once every 16 cycles (max stall 15). Root cause: the 3 bounded-liveness assertions `slot{0,1,2}_progress_valid_ready_issued_within_16` fail because the formal solver can keep `exeReady` stuck at `00` forever, preventing any instruction from ever issuing — yet the DUT issue logic is correct (issue signals are legitimately gated by exeReady). The fix adds `exeReadyStallCount` (RegInit 0.U(5.W)), incremented when neither exeReady(0) nor exeReady(1) is asserted and reset to 0 on any fire, with `assume(exeReadyStallCount < 16.U)`. This is tight enough for the 16-cycle liveness bound (max stall 15 means a ready instruction waits at most 15 cycles for exeReady, well within the 16-cycle deadline). All three failing properties are addressed by this single environmental fix. Action: new fairness assumption block inserted between opsReady stability assumptions and bounded-liveness assertions."
  ],
